{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MinPlusValuationBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MinPlusValuationBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Monoid.Unbundled.WithTop","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.WithBot","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.minVal_singleton_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.minVal_singleton_eq","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MinPlusValuationBound.lean#L110-L115","doc":"The one-dimensional case has nothing to cancel against: a single-term sum\nattains the bound with equality.  So strictness is a genuinely\nmulti-dimensional phenomenon, matching the measurement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.exists_strict_of_cancel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.exists_strict_of_cancel","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MinPlusValuationBound.lean#L93-L108","doc":"**Non-vacuity: the bound can be STRICT.**  Two terms of equal finite\nvaluation can cancel, sending the sum's valuation to `⊤`.  This is the measured\nfailure mode — two of forty-six (word, λ) pairs, both on channels of dimension\n`> 1`, where the minimal paths cancel and the min-plus value under-states the\ntrue valuation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sumVal_eq_val_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sumVal_eq_val_prod","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MinPlusValuationBound.lean#L83-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sumVal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sumVal","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MinPlusValuationBound.lean#L76-L81","doc":"The sum of valuations along one path — the \"plus\" of min-plus.  A\nmultiplicative valuation turns a product of entries into a sum of integers,\nwhich is why each path contributes a single integer weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.pathProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.pathProd","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MinPlusValuationBound.lean#L69-L74","doc":"Product along a path.  Defined here rather than imported: `List.sum` is\navailable in this build but `List.prod` is not, and a local definition keeps the\nimport surface minimal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.minVal_le_val_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.minVal_le_val_sum","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MinPlusValuationBound.lean#L54-L67","doc":"**The bound.**  For a non-archimedean valuation, the valuation of a sum is\nat least the minimum of the valuations of its terms.  This is what makes the\nmin-plus matrix product a valid lower bound on `val(χ)`, hence a valid UPPER\nbound on the pole order — and it is only a bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.minVal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.minVal","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MinPlusValuationBound.lean#L49-L52","doc":"The minimum valuation over a list of terms — the \"min\" of min-plus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Val","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Val","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MinPlusValuationBound.lean#L44-L45","doc":"Valuations take values in `ℤ ∪ {⊤}`, with `⊤` the valuation of zero. ","signatureChunk":0}]}